This code reads a single string input from the user and determines whether it is a single uppercase letter (A-Z) or a single lowercase letter (a-z), printing **"A"** if it matches an uppercase letter or **"a"** if it matches a lowercase letter.

## How It Works

Despite its heavily obfuscated appearance, the code is functionally equivalent to a simple check like:
```java
if (input.length() == 1 && Character.isUpperCase(input.charAt(0))) {
    System.out.println("A");
} else if (input.length() == 1 && Character.isLowerCase(input.charAt(0))) {
    System.out.println("a");
}
```

